``dials.index``, ``dials.stills_process``: when ``known_symmetry.unit_cell`` is given, apply the known space group in the setting that reproduces that cell. Previously the setting was chosen by Le Page delta alone, so a lattice with more metric symmetry than the space group (e.g. a monoclinic cell with beta close to 90 degrees) could have its symmetry axis assigned to a different lattice axis on different images, producing several permuted unit cell populations from one crystal form.
